# The interchange and functional group envelope, the same in every version Trenova reads.
# ISA11 is the repetition separator from 00402 on and the standards identifier `U` before;
# the envelope reader handles that position itself, so it is defined loosely here.

segment ISA | Interchange Control Header
  I01 ID 2/2 M | Authorization Information Qualifier
  I02 AN 10/10 M | Authorization Information
  I03 ID 2/2 M | Security Information Qualifier
  I04 AN 10/10 M | Security Information
  I05 ID 2/2 M | Interchange ID Qualifier
  I06 AN 15/15 M | Interchange Sender ID
  I05 ID 2/2 M | Interchange ID Qualifier
  I07 AN 15/15 M | Interchange Receiver ID
  I08 DT 6/6 M | Interchange Date
  I09 TM 4/4 M | Interchange Time
  I65 AN 1/1 M | Repetition Separator
  I11 ID 5/5 M | Interchange Control Version Number
  I12 N0 9/9 M | Interchange Control Number
  I13 ID 1/1 M | Acknowledgment Requested
  I14 ID 1/1 M | Interchange Usage Indicator
  I15 AN 1/1 M | Component Element Separator

segment IEA | Interchange Control Trailer
  I16 N0 1/5 M | Number of Included Functional Groups
  I12 N0 9/9 M | Interchange Control Number

segment TA1 | Interchange Acknowledgment
  I12 N0 9/9 M | Interchange Control Number
  I08 DT 6/6 M | Interchange Date
  I09 TM 4/4 M | Interchange Time
  I17 ID 1/1 M | Interchange Acknowledgment Code
  I18 ID 3/3 M | Interchange Note Code

segment GS | Functional Group Header
  479 ID 2/2 M | Functional Identifier Code
  142 AN 2/15 M | Application Sender's Code
  124 AN 2/15 M | Application Receiver's Code
  373 DT 8/8 M | Date
  337 TM 4/8 M | Time
  28 N0 1/9 M | Group Control Number
  455 ID 1/2 M | Responsible Agency Code
  480 AN 1/12 M | Version / Release / Industry Identifier Code

segment GE | Functional Group Trailer
  97 N0 1/6 M | Number of Transaction Sets Included
  28 N0 1/9 M | Group Control Number

codes I01 | Authorization Information Qualifier
  00 | No Authorization Information Present
  01 | UCS Communications ID
  02 | EDX Communications ID
  03 | Additional Data Identification
  04 | Rail Communications ID
  05 | Department of Defense (DoD) Communication Identifier
  06 | United States Federal Government Communication Identifier

codes I03 | Security Information Qualifier
  00 | No Security Information Present
  01 | Password

codes I13 | Acknowledgment Requested
  0 | No Interchange Acknowledgment Requested
  1 | Interchange Acknowledgment Requested (TA1)

codes I14 | Interchange Usage Indicator
  I | Information
  P | Production Data
  T | Test Data

codes I17 | Interchange Acknowledgment Code
  A | The Transmitted Interchange Control Structure Header and Trailer Have Been Received and Have No Errors
  E | The Transmitted Interchange Control Structure Header and Trailer Have Been Received and Are Accepted But Errors Are Noted
  R | The Transmitted Interchange Control Structure Header and Trailer are Rejected Because of Errors

codes 455 | Responsible Agency Code
  T | Transportation Data Coordinating Committee (TDCC)
  X | Accredited Standards Committee X12
